according to nissan it engineered the  second generation of the note in europe  for europe technical goodies are packed  into plenty in the sporty hatch to  guarantee carefree city driving  it's testing hard today it's based on  the renault clio's platform says our car  tester carla siemens  visually it strikes a decidedly new note  the contours swing down under the grille  an emblem flanked by multi-reflector  headlights  the big-eyed daytime running lights  blend the note and almost playful air  the elegant flowing contours and the  windows swept up toward the rear give it  a dynamic sporty look  the all-round monitor works with four  separate cameras one in front one behind  and two on the sides  there are blind spot and lane departure  warning systems plus another assist that  spots moving objects when reversing  together they comprise nissan's very own  degree safety shield  and how does nissan's new city car  perform on the road  karola describes it as small nimble and  easy to drive with the instruments all  neatly arranged on the downside she has  the feeling that the note doesn't have a  lot of pickup putting the pedal to the  metal doesn't do much  but the nissan note does well enough  driving around town three engines are  available two gasoline powered and one  diesel  this model puts out 59 kilowatts of  power and fuel consumption is rated at  4.7 liters per hundred kilometers it can  zip along country highways at a top  speed of 170 kilometers per hour  the interior emphasizes ease of  operation and simplicity  a nice detail is the eco button  pressing it brings up the ecometer in  the speedometer it's supposed to  motivate the driver to drive more fuel  consciously  the note's rear bench has sufficient  room for passengers and a bit of extra  cargo but the bags can just as easily go  into the trunk the double decker  configuration can expand the storage  volume from 325 to 411 leaders  sums up the nissan note as a dependable  and robust city run around that  definitely lives up to the compact car  idea the interior could have stood a few  improvements here and there mostly in  the instrument panel she's not entirely  happy with the materials and workmanship  the prevalence of hard plastic isn't to  her taste  in terms of safety though the note is an  innovator the safety shield however only  enters the picture with the mid-range  equipment levels and costs around 1200  euros extra
 

